ough: it shows Notepad instructions alongside an advertising-platform campaign setup, channel selection, scheduling, and funding screens.", "frame_ids": ["F0024", "F0030", "F0035", "F0041", "F0047", "F0053", "F0058"]}]}, "annotation": {"binary_label": "Non-scam", "primary_subtype": "N03", "content_role": "promotion_or_instruction", "contextual_rationale": "This video is non-scam content because it presents a tutorial or walkthrough for configuring an advertising campaign intended to generate tech-support calls. Its payment requirement and claims about campaign approval and call volume are described as terms of an advertising service, while the available material does not establish deception, false claims, completed payment, delivered results, or victim loss.", "fine_grained_rationale": "The primary observable context is an operational walkthrough showing how to configure advertising-platform campaign settings, channels, targeting, and scheduling.", "evidence": [{"evidence_id": "E001", "observation": "The title identifies the subject as generating inbound tech-support calls.", "source_id": "TITLE_0001", "quote": "How to Generate Inbound Calls for Tech Support"}, {"evidence_id": "E002", "observation": "The description discusses pop-up advertising as an online advertising method.", "source_id": "DESCRIPTION_0001", "quote": "Pop-up ads or popups are a form of online advertising on the World Wide Web intended to increase web traffic or capture email addresses."}, {"evidence_id": "E003", "observation": "A browser displays an advertising campaign setup form with fields for campaign name, advertising URL, bid limits, daily limit, traffic network, and submission.", "source_id": "F0030", "quote": ""}, {"evidence_id": "E004", "observation": "Instructional notes are shown alongside an advertising-platform scheduling page, including channel selections and campaign scheduling.", "source_id": "F0047", "quote": ""}]}}
